"""Every code listing of the SEN0401 chapter 6 deck 2.1.0 (remedy of 2026-10-22, over examples_v2_0_0.py, which is kept as the earlier draft) and the source of the chapter-code
manifest that the page's chapter-code tab reads. One entry per code slide, in SLIDE ORDER. A listing is a list of GROUPS; a group is a few single-line statements and the plain-language
note that explains them (the deck standard asks for an explanation beside every code box). Every statement is ONE line, because the deck's own check re-runs each '>>> ' row of a slide, one
paragraph at a time, in one namespace after the PRELUDE. The last row of a listing is an expression (`final`, which is also in `show`): the slide prints its value under it, the only
REPL text of the slide; the full result of the example is drawn as a chart or a table beside the listing from the recorded `show` values (examples_run_v2_1_0.py), never typed.
A statement is at most 58 characters, so that a code line never wraps (deck standard D12)."""
